    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "AAAAUX/++20\u003d",
        "filename": "keystone/common/cache/backends/mongo.py",
        "patchSetId": 16
      },
      "lineNbr": 366,
      "author": {
        "id": 1091
      },
      "writtenOn": "2014-02-17T20:42:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Key is cache client generated content so there is no way to know what kind of data or format it will have. That\u0027s why avoided \u0027key\u0027 field value as index.\n\nIn earlier mongodb docs, it was recommended to use _id values that are roughly in ascending order. If the _id\u0027s are in a somewhat well defined order, on inserts the entire b-tree for the _id index need not be loaded. BSON ObjectIds have this property.",
      "parentUuid": "AAAAUX//Ja4\u003d",
      "revId": "834afbb1bf242b7f4ea618ee71d9dcf54ad23744",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
